    "created_at": "2025-06-06T20:55:56Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-06-06T20:59:07Z",
    "body": "@domfarolino what you wrote completely describes my understanding. As far as I know, the IDL specification describes [creation of platform objects](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#new) And when creating a platform object, the Realm must be explicitly passed. But the HTML specification does not explicitly specify that the window object must use the [new](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#new) definition from IDL.\n\n@annevk it's a pity that such an important part of the HTML specification has such a problem.\n\n---\n\n@domfarolino @annevk I remembered one more thing:\n> The [Window](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/nav-history-apis.html#window) object has an **associated Document**, which is a [Document](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#document) object. It is set when the [Window](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/nav-history-apis.html#window) object is created, and only ever changed during [navigation](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsing-the-web.html#navigate) from the [initial about:blank](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#is-initial-about:blank) [Document](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#document).\n\nThe [create a new browsing context and document](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/document-sequences.html#creating-a-new-browsing-context) algorithm does not have an explicit setting of the [associated Document](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/nav-history-apis.html#concept-document-window) for window, due to the fact that window is not defined in the algorithm at all. As I understand it, this case is the same as window and it is implicitly set after document is created?",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
